    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0119" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister Churchill
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d19-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-02">May 2, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>To the Former Naval Person from the President personal and secret No. 275.</p>
                <p>I am really delighted you are coming. I agree most heartily that we have some
                    important business to settle at once; the sooner the better. Marshall and King
                    have postponed their Pacific trip. I want you of course to stay here with
                    me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d19-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d19-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, London, via Navy channels at 4:05
                    p.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
